  },
  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;be an integer such that all the real roots of the polynomial&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></math> lie in the interval <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Then, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>|</mo></math> is equal to ______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Now <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>Hence <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> has a root in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Further <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfenced><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;for all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;belongs to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is strictly increasing function. Since it is an odd degree polynomial it will have exactly one real root.</p><p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> has only one real root, so <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>a</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
